meta {
  name: Get Service By Vehicle ID
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/service/vehicle/:vehicle_id
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  vehicle_id: e1288783-a5d4-1c4c-2cd6-0e92f7cc3bf9
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Get Service By Vehicle ID

  This request is used to get all service history. This request interacts with the MySQL database, and has a protected routes.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Name       | Type   | Required | Description | Example                               |
  |------------|--------|----------|--------------|------------------------------------------|
  | vehicle_id | string | yes      | Vehicle ID  | e1288783-a5d4-1c4c-2cd6-0e92f7cc3bf9   |

  ## Responses

  **200 — Service fetched successfully.** Ordered in descending order by `remind_at` and `created_at`
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "service fetched",
    "data": [
      {
        "service_category": "Routine",
        "service_note": "Lorem ipsum",
        "service_price_total": 15000000,
        "service_location": "Honda Tandean",
        "created_at": "2024-09-20 22:53:47",
        "remind_at": "2024-09-20 22:53:47"
      }
    ]
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
```

  **404 — service failed to fetched**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "service not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}